    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an email-uniqueness rule to `POST /api/owners` that rejects a new owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, responding with **409 Conflict**. I mirrored the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern exactly.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckEmailUnique.java` \u2014 reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` (email already lower-cased by `ValidateNewOwner`), and compares its lower-cased email against every existing owner's lower-cased email, throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a collision. Email is optional, so null/blank requests skip the check.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the offending email.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with an RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` and an `errors: [\"email\"]` property, consistent with the other handlers.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 routes the escalation to the handler.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkEmailUnique` step (governed by `transaction`) after `checkTelephoneUnique` and before `checkHouseholdUnique`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
